# MAGIC <div class="hero"><div class="blob b1"></div><div class="blob b2"></div><div class="blob b3"></div><div class="hero-in"><div class="kicker">Advanced Data Engineering with Databricks</div><h1><span class="kicker-inline">Recap</span>Databricks Streaming and Lakeflow Spark Declarative Pipelines</h1><div class="chips"><span class="chip">Course 1 of 4</span><span class="chip">⏱ ~9 minutes</span></div><p class="sub">Production streaming: how <strong>Structured Streaming</strong> keeps state, emits results and recovers, and how <strong>declarative pipelines</strong> apply it to ingestion, joins, deduplication and <strong>CDC</strong>.</p></div></div><div class="idea"><span class="idea-icon">💡</span><div><b>The one idea to remember:</b> a stream is an <strong>unbounded table</strong> processed incrementally. <strong>Checkpoints</strong> make it exactly-once, <strong>watermarks</strong> bound its state, and declarative pipelines manage most of this for you.</div></div>
