# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">03</span><span class="sec-icon">🧠</span><h2>State, windows and watermarks</h2></div><pre class="diagram">tumbling  |----|----|----|      fixed, non-overlapping: &quot;per 5 minutes&quot;
# MAGIC sliding   |------|               overlapping: &quot;last 10 minutes, every 5 minutes&quot;
# MAGIC             |------|
# MAGIC session   |--|   |-----|         gap-based: &quot;activity bursts per user&quot;</pre>
# MAGIC <ul>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Stateless</strong> operations (<code>select</code>, <code>filter</code>, stream-static join) don't remember anything between micro-batches.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Stateful</strong> operations (aggregations, <code>dropDuplicates</code>, stream-stream joins) keep <strong>state</strong> in the state store (RocksDB), and it is saved in the checkpoint.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Watermark</strong> = the latest event time seen minus the allowed delay. Windows older than the watermark are <strong>finalized</strong> and their state is <strong>dropped</strong>. Events arriving later than that can be ignored.</li>
# MAGIC <li>A longer delay accepts later data, but keeps <strong>more state</strong> and delays append-mode output.</li>
# MAGIC <li>Changing the aggregation keys, the window, or the number of stateful operators requires a <strong>new checkpoint</strong>.</li>
# MAGIC </ul>
# MAGIC </div>

