# MAGIC <div class="dbx">
# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">04</span><span class="sec-icon">🌊</span><h2>Streaming joins and deduplication</h2></div><div class="tbl"><table>
# MAGIC <thead>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <th>Join</th>
# MAGIC <th>How it works</th>
# MAGIC <th>Watch out</th>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC </thead>
# MAGIC <tbody>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Stream-static</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>Each micro-batch joins with the <strong>current</strong> version of a Delta table</td>
# MAGIC <td>Dimension changes are <strong>not</strong> re-applied to past results. Use an MV when results must stay correct</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Stream-stream</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>Both sides buffered in state until they can match</td>
# MAGIC <td>Needs <strong>watermarks on both sides</strong> plus a <strong>time-range condition</strong>, otherwise state grows forever</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC </tbody>
# MAGIC </table></div>
# MAGIC <div class="code"><div class="code-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="lang">PYTHON</span><button class="copy" type="button">copy</button></div><pre><span style="color: #E6EDF3">deduped</span> <span style="color: #FF7B72; font-weight: bold">=</span> <span style="color: #E6EDF3">(events</span>
# MAGIC     <span style="color: #FF7B72; font-weight: bold">.</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">withWatermark(</span><span style="color: #A5D6FF">"event_ts"</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">,</span> <span style="color: #A5D6FF">"1 hour"</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">)</span>
# MAGIC     <span style="color: #FF7B72; font-weight: bold">.</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">dropDuplicatesWithinWatermark([</span><span style="color: #A5D6FF">"event_id"</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">]))</span>   <span style="color: #8B949E; font-style: italic"># bounded state</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #8B949E; font-style: italic"># dropDuplicates(["event_id"]) without a watermark keeps every key forever</span></pre></div>
# MAGIC <p><strong><code>foreachBatch</code></strong> runs batch code per micro-batch, e.g. a <code>MERGE</code> into Delta or writes to several sinks. It is at-least-once, so make it <strong>idempotent</strong> (MERGE is), and deduplicate inside the batch first.</p>
# MAGIC </div>

