# MAGIC <span style="color: #E6EDF3">)</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">AS</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">SELECT</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">payload:device_id::string</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">AS</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">device_id,</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">payload:temp::double</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">AS</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">temp,</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #6E7681">            </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">payload:ts::</span><span style="color: #FF7B72">timestamp</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">AS</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">event_ts</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #FF7B72">FROM</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">STREAM(events_bronze);</span></pre></div>
# MAGIC <ul>
# MAGIC <li>Pipelines manage <strong>checkpoints, retries and the schema location</strong> for you.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Append flows</strong>: several sources (e.g. one Kafka topic per region) write into one streaming table, and backfills run as a separate <code>ONCE</code> flow.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Quarantine</strong>: route rows that fail a rule into a separate table instead of dropping them silently.</li>
# MAGIC <li>Use a <strong>materialized view</strong> for aggregates that must reflect late updates. A streaming table processes each row only once.</li>
# MAGIC <li>A streaming read <strong>fails</strong> if its source table gets UPDATEs or DELETEs. Use <code>skipChangeCommits</code> or read the <strong>change data feed</strong>.</li>
# MAGIC </ul>
# MAGIC </div>

